-- Insurance claim settlement (v0).
--
-- An insurer authorises claim settlements against a policy. Every
-- settlement consumes from the policy's aggregate limit; once the
-- aggregate is exhausted, no further settlements admit. The audit log
-- records who decided each payment, when, against which policy, and
-- under what authority.
--
-- The load-bearing rule is the cumulative-cap shape:
--
--   sum(already_paid_on_policy) + proposed_settlement <= aggregate_limit
--
-- This is the IR shape Expr::Add was added for. Without Add the rule
-- would have to be written as `proposed <= aggregate - already_paid`,
-- which works but contorts the natural business statement.
--
-- The proposing actor is *transition context*, not a transformation
-- parameter. authorise_settlement declares no `actor` parameter; the
-- proposing actor is consulted via $actor inside the require for
-- authority and stamped onto the SettlementAuthorised record.

-- ============================================================
-- Invariant: payment must have authorisation.
--
-- An eternal consistency rule. The transformation never asserts a
-- SettlementPaid without an authorisation, but the runtime contract
-- holds against candidate state regardless of how it arrived. An
-- orphan payment is rejected by this invariant; a real corruption
-- scenario surfaces immediately rather than persisting silently.
-- ============================================================
invariant paid_implies_authorised:
    SettlementPaid(_, claim, settlement, amount) implies
        SettlementAuthorised(claim, settlement, amount, _)

-- ============================================================
-- Open a policy with an aggregate limit.
-- ============================================================
transformation issue_policy(policy_id, aggregate_limit):
    assert Policy(policy_id, aggregate_limit)
    emit PolicyIssued(policy_id)

-- ============================================================
-- Record a reported loss against a policy. The policy must exist;
-- the claimed amount is informational - cumulative-cap reads from
-- SettlementPaid, not from this claim.
-- ============================================================
transformation report_claim(claim_id, policy_id, claimed_amount):
    require Policy(policy_id, _)
    assert ClaimReported(claim_id, policy_id, claimed_amount)
    emit ClaimReported(claim_id)

-- ============================================================
-- Grant settlement authority. Ungated in v0; administrative
-- authority for granting is out of scope.
-- ============================================================
transformation grant_settlement_authority(actor, limit):
    assert SettlementAuthority(actor, limit)
    emit SettlementAuthorityGranted(actor, limit)

-- ============================================================
-- The load-bearing transformation. Authorises a settlement against
-- a reported claim, subject to:
--
--   1. The proposing actor's settlement authority covers the
--      proposed amount.
--   2. The cumulative-cap rule holds against the policy aggregate.
--
-- The Let bindings pull policy_id and aggregate_limit into scope so
-- the cumulative-cap require can reference both. Stmt::Require is a
-- yes/no gate that does not propagate its match's bindings back into
-- the active scope - which is why value extraction goes through Let
-- and ValueOf rather than through the existence requires alone.
-- ============================================================
transformation authorise_settlement(claim_id, settlement_id, amount):
    -- gate: the claim was reported
    require ClaimReported(claim_id, _, _)

    -- extract policy_id from the reported claim, then aggregate_limit
    -- from the policy. The Policy ValueOf needs no separate guard
    -- because report_claim already ensured the policy exists.
    let policy_id = value_of ClaimReported(claim_id, _, _)
    let aggregate_limit = value_of Policy(policy_id, _)

    -- actor authority gate
    require SettlementAuthority($actor, actor_limit)
        and amount <= actor_limit

    -- cumulative-cap gate (the Expr::Add shape)
    require sum { paid | SettlementPaid(policy_id, _, _, paid) }
                + amount
            <= aggregate_limit

    assert SettlementAuthorised(claim_id, settlement_id, amount, $actor)
    assert SettlementPaid(policy_id, claim_id, settlement_id, amount)
    emit ClaimPaymentRequested(settlement_id, amount, $actor)

-- ============================================================
-- Derived claim: cumulative paid per policy.
--
-- Enumerated on demand via `morpholog inspect derived
-- insurance_claim_settlement PolicyLimitUsage`. As-of replay
-- reconstructs the usage as it stood at any prior transition.
-- ============================================================
derived PolicyLimitUsage(policy_id):
    used = sum { paid | SettlementPaid(policy_id, _, _, paid) }
    over SettlementPaid(policy_id, _, _, _)
